  "id": "COMPOUND:32420 - PROTEIN:717",
  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C is implicated in modulating the ATP-binding cassette sub-family C member 9 (ABCC9) through two distinct pathways. The first pathway involves Oblonganoside C targeting Serine/threonine-protein kinase ICK, which is then targeted by Ent-Gloeosteretriol, ultimately leading to ABCC9 inhibition. The second pathway links Oblonganoside C to Serine/threonine-protein kinase SBK1, which is targeted by benzocaine, also resulting in ABCC9 modulation. Both pathways converge on ABCC9, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Oblonganoside C influences ABCC9 function. The integration of these two pathways highlights the possibility of a dual mechanism involving kinase activity and direct interaction with ABCC9. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Oblonganoside C and ABCC9, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
